You either eat a shit ton of food.

00:41:28.544 --> 00:41:29.888
It didn't really care about the quality.

00:41:29.888 --> 00:41:33.073
- But there are a lot
of Indian Curry buffets

00:41:33.073 --> 00:41:35.276
because in SF certain areas.

00:41:35.276 --> 00:41:37.741
- Pretty much every buffet in
the UK has Indian Curry in it.

00:41:37.741 --> 00:41:38.574
- Oh really?
- I'm gonna be honest there,

00:41:38.574 --> 00:41:39.407
they're pretty bad though.

00:41:39.407 --> 00:41:42.085
They're really fucking bad.

00:41:42.085 --> 00:41:44.492
- I would argue that pretty like 90,

00:41:44.492 --> 00:41:45.825
actually I don't think I've ever been

00:41:45.825 --> 00:41:47.335
to a good buffet place in the UK.

00:41:47.335 --> 00:41:49.889
In terms of like, this is good food.

00:41:49.889 --> 00:41:51.713
You go there, to eat a shit ton of food,

00:41:51.713 --> 00:41:53.067
and you trick your brain,

00:41:53.067 --> 00:41:54.209
into thinking it tastes good

00:41:54.209 --> 00:41:55.042
because you're eating so much food.

00:41:55.042 --> 00:41:58.813
But in reality it just tastes like shit.

00:41:58.813 --> 00:41:59.646
- I think that's most buffets.

00:41:59.646 --> 00:42:01.018
(all laughing)

00:42:01.018 --> 00:42:03.541
- I'll just hate like
the whole plate situation

00:42:03.541 --> 00:42:04.452
with buffets.

00:42:04.452 --> 00:42:05.962
Because when you get a dish right,

00:42:05.962 --> 00:42:07.290
that you've hand selected,

00:42:07.290 --> 00:42:09.573
it's normally perfectly
fit for that plate.

00:42:09.573 --> 00:42:11.841
When you start going around the buffet

00:42:11.841 --> 00:42:12.674
and you start putting things on,

00:42:12.674 --> 00:42:14.615
I don't want some of the foods touching.

00:42:14.615 --> 00:42:15.448
- Yeah.

00:42:15.448 --> 00:42:17.817
- And I hate that because I'm like,

00:42:17.817 --> 00:42:21.406
I don't want the saucy
dish to touch the thing

00:42:21.406 --> 00:42:22.574
that's supposed to be like dry.

00:42:22.574 --> 00:42:25.553
- Yeah.
- So it's kind of a mess.

00:42:25.553 --> 00:42:27.106
But if there is sauce, it's like,

00:42:27.106 --> 00:42:28.280
all right, if this dish
has a lot of sauce,

00:42:28.280 --> 00:42:29.953
how do I kind of like integrate

00:42:29.953 --> 00:42:33.585
this with my other food
selection on my plate?

00:42:33.585 --> 00:42:35.587
- I have honestly never
cared because I'm like,

00:42:35.587 --> 00:42:37.311
at the end of the day, this is
all going to turn into shit.

00:42:37.311 --> 00:42:39.258
So, it doesn't matter to me.

00:42:39.258 --> 00:42:43.731
(speakers arguing indistinctly)

00:42:43.731 --> 00:42:44.564
- You just get a new plate.

00:42:44.564 --> 00:42:47.082
- You can't just say whatever
goes in your mouth is shit,

00:42:47.082 --> 00:42:48.351
so why give a fuck.

00:42:48.351 --> 00:42:49.184
- I actually don't.

00:42:49.184 --> 00:42:50.234
- 'Cause like I'm the guy at the buffet.

00:42:50.234 --> 00:42:52.935
- You should just eat
like cement. (laughs)

00:42:52.935 --> 00:42:53.981
- I'm like the guy at the buffet,

00:42:53.981 --> 00:42:54.814
who has like fucking three
different plates. Right?

00:42:54.814 --> 00:42:57.227
Because somethings you can't mix.

00:42:57.227 --> 00:42:59.554
- I take that right.

00:42:59.554 --> 00:43:01.231
I go and get another plate to make sure

00:43:01.231 --> 00:43:02.314
that the dishes are right.

00:43:02.314 --> 00:43:03.310
- You don't get the food, put it down,

00:43:03.310 --> 00:43:04.156
eat it and then go again?

00:43:04.156 --> 00:43:04.989
- No, no.

00:43:04.989 --> 00:43:06.227
- No, because that's too much effort.

00:43:06.227 --> 00:43:07.060
- What if you change your mind though

00:43:07.060 --> 00:43:10.492
after you eat the first food?
- Just throw it away.

00:43:10.492 --> 00:43:12.187
- It's all gonna get thrown out anyway.

00:43:12.187 --> 00:43:13.694
- What if you take your
standard instead of taking

00:43:13.694 --> 00:43:15.560
too much of something starchy,

00:43:15.560 --> 00:43:18.050
and I've been like,
"Shit I can't eat this."

00:43:18.050 --> 00:43:19.305
This is prime real estate in my stomach.

00:43:19.305 --> 00:43:21.121
I can't have another bread roll.

00:43:21.121 --> 00:43:22.829
So I just leave it.
- 'Cause in Vegas apparently.

00:43:22.829 --> 00:43:24.662
- I never get bread, when I'm in a buffet.

00:43:24.662 --> 00:43:26.143
You mad man.
- I'm kidding-

00:43:26.143 --> 00:43:27.604
- Cause in Vegas apparently it's a law now

00:43:27.604 --> 00:43:30.096
that all the buffet places
at the end of every day,

00:43:30.096 --> 00:43:33.346
they have to throw out like everything,

00:43:34.393 --> 00:43:36.585
because there was this
lawsuit that dead ass,

00:43:36.585 --> 00:43:37.418
I read about this.

00:43:37.418 --> 00:43:38.708
There was this lawsuit that
happened a couple of years ago,

00:43:38.708 --> 00:43:42.213
where they kept some of the food,

00:43:42.213 --> 00:43:44.620
and like stored it in like the behind,

00:43:44.620 --> 00:43:47.451
like the stare and some
homeless guy came up,

00:43:47.451 --> 00:43:48.916
ate it, got food poisoning,

00:43:48.916 --> 00:43:50.919
sued the buffet place and won.

00:43:50.919 --> 00:43:51.752
- What?

00:43:51.752 --> 00:43:52.937
- Well hopefully he got a nice home.

00:43:52.937 --> 00:43:53.770
- Yeah.
- What?

00:43:53.770 --> 00:43:55.164
- Yeah.
- what?

00:43:55.164 --> 00:43:56.997
- And so now in Vegas,

00:43:58.703 --> 00:44:00.026
I don't know about the
whole state of Nevada,

00:44:00.026 --> 00:44:01.715
but in Vegas every buffet place,

00:44:01.715 --> 00:44:04.803
legally has to throw out
every single food that's left

00:44:04.803 --> 00:44:06.203
on that day and make
it fresh the next day.

00:44:06.203 --> 00:44:08.649
So, I can't imagine how much
food that's thrown away.

00:44:08.649 --> 00:44:09.502
- I mean that's good for customers though

00:44:09.502 --> 00:44:11.044
but unfortunately terrible for-

00:44:11.044 --> 00:44:13.714
- It's also a waste of
a shit load of food.

00:44:13.714 --> 00:44:14.865
- You'd wish they'd just gave it away

00:44:14.865 --> 00:44:15.698
but it's logistically it's quite hard

00:44:15.698 --> 00:44:17.834
to just give away a lot of food.

00:44:17.834 --> 00:44:19.046
- Like donate it to the shelters?

00:44:19.046 --> 00:44:20.222
- [Men] Yeah.

00:44:20.222 --> 00:44:22.599
- I think some coffee chains in the UK,

00:44:22.599 --> 00:44:24.294
especially London, I
think like Pret does it,

00:44:24.294 --> 00:44:25.357
where like at the end of the day,

00:44:25.357 --> 00:44:26.519
someone will come in and
get all the sandwiches

00:44:26.519 --> 00:44:28.597
that didn't sell and then that night go

00:44:28.597 --> 00:44:29.611
and take them to homeless people.

00:44:29.611 --> 00:44:30.444
- Yeah.
- oh yeah.

00:44:30.444 --> 00:44:31.400
So that makes more sense.
- So they're still lucky

00:44:31.400 --> 00:44:32.983
to eat.
That's good.

00:44:34.609 --> 00:44:38.060
- I am curious, as like
the resident American here.

00:44:38.060 --> 00:44:38.893
- Oh, yeah.

00:44:38.893 --> 00:44:40.345
- Well I'm the only American.

00:44:40.345 --> 00:44:41.178
- Pretty much the only American -

00:44:41.178 --> 00:44:42.452
- You're the only American in the office?

00:44:42.452 --> 00:44:45.099
- Yeah right, apart from Sydney.

00:44:45.099 --> 00:44:46.163
- Yeah.

00:44:46.163 --> 00:44:47.538
- But Sydney doesn't count.

00:44:47.538 --> 00:44:48.471
