00:44:55.421 --> 00:44:56.779
and you're just off-camera listening?

00:44:56.779 --> 00:44:58.747
- I'm just like, that's true.

00:44:58.747 --> 00:45:00.074
(all laughing)

00:45:00.074 --> 00:45:01.324
- Confirmation.

00:45:02.993 --> 00:45:03.951
- Almost the same thing.

00:45:03.951 --> 00:45:05.087
- Yeah, you have been wrong,

00:45:05.087 --> 00:45:05.977
but I'm just saying, "Ah whatever."

00:45:05.977 --> 00:45:07.621
It means everything.

00:45:07.621 --> 00:45:09.897
- Yeah, we rank on about our
own countries just as much.

00:45:09.897 --> 00:45:11.091
- Yeah and then also Americans will rag

00:45:11.091 --> 00:45:14.763
on your countries and whatnot.
- Yeah, of course.

00:45:14.763 --> 00:45:17.814
- It's interesting though 'cause
most of my foreign friends

00:45:17.814 --> 00:45:20.109
are usually American,

00:45:20.109 --> 00:45:21.817
and it's interesting hearing,

00:45:21.817 --> 00:45:24.529
non-Americans talk about
Americans that I know.

00:45:24.529 --> 00:45:25.712
- Has there ever been a time though

00:45:25.712 --> 00:45:28.165
where you were just like,
"No, that's so wrong.

00:45:28.165 --> 00:45:29.630
I don't wanna tell them."

00:45:29.630 --> 00:45:32.849
- There are a few times but I just forgot.

00:45:32.849 --> 00:45:34.762
I mean the one that
sticks out is the butter

00:45:34.762 --> 00:45:36.262
or the lard thing.

00:45:37.199 --> 00:45:38.567
Joey, you were saying
that there's someplace

00:45:38.567 --> 00:45:39.850
that they put lard on
popcorn or something.

00:45:39.850 --> 00:45:40.683
- Yeah.

00:45:40.683 --> 00:45:42.547
- I've never heard of that. (laughs)

00:45:42.547 --> 00:45:45.077
- Did we ever find out where
that was or was it a lie?

00:45:45.077 --> 00:45:45.925
- I don't know.
- I have no idea

00:45:45.925 --> 00:45:47.051
but I was like, "What?"

00:45:47.051 --> 00:45:49.139
- It's not a lie because
I saw it with my own eyes.

00:45:49.139 --> 00:45:49.972
(Garnt laughing)

00:45:49.972 --> 00:45:51.959
So it's like, it's not a lie.

00:45:51.959 --> 00:45:53.182
Maybe it was that cinema, I don't know,

00:45:53.182 --> 00:45:55.446
but I saw it.
- In Vegas?

00:45:55.446 --> 00:45:58.448
- Yeah, it's probably
not like a common thing.

00:45:58.448 --> 00:46:01.493
- With melted butter is
definitely a common thing.

00:46:01.493 --> 00:46:02.326
- Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:46:02.326 --> 00:46:03.594
- Did you speak to many non-Americans

00:46:03.594 --> 00:46:05.234
who speak English before?

00:46:05.234 --> 00:46:06.608
- Non-Americans who speak English.

00:46:06.608 --> 00:46:07.525
- In Japan?

00:46:08.507 --> 00:46:10.370
- Like Koreans?

00:46:10.370 --> 00:46:11.786
- I guess so yeah.

00:46:11.786 --> 00:46:14.567
- Is there a big difference
between Americans

00:46:14.567 --> 00:46:15.786
and non-Americans?

00:46:15.786 --> 00:46:17.542
- The way you guys talk,

00:46:17.542 --> 00:46:19.913
some things you say and
then I end up saying it.

00:46:19.913 --> 00:46:21.315
I'm like-
(Garnt laughing)

00:46:21.315 --> 00:46:22.627
- Like what?

00:46:22.627 --> 00:46:24.110
- I don't know.

00:46:24.110 --> 00:46:24.943
- Like the time that
I almost convinced you

00:46:24.943 --> 00:46:25.952
that the Australian
currency was the way it is.

00:46:25.952 --> 00:46:28.032
- Yeah, I didn't believe you,

00:46:28.032 --> 00:46:30.931
I was just being polite to your friends.

00:46:30.931 --> 00:46:32.002
(all laughing)

00:46:32.002 --> 00:46:33.183
- So at Smash, which is
the convention in Sydney.

00:46:33.183 --> 00:46:35.490
The anime one.
- A few years ago.

00:46:35.490 --> 00:46:37.059
- Yeah, so I got invited as a guest

00:46:37.059 --> 00:46:38.259
and Meilyne came with me.

00:46:38.259 --> 00:46:39.450
- Yeah.
- And,

00:46:39.450 --> 00:46:40.641
my friend from uni was there.

00:46:40.641 --> 00:46:42.596
I invited them,

00:46:42.596 --> 00:46:44.838
and I don't know how we
got onto the conversation,

00:46:44.838 --> 00:46:47.421
but my friend dead ass
almost convinced Meilyne

00:46:47.421 --> 00:46:50.206
that the Australian currency
was called dollarydoos.

00:46:50.206 --> 00:46:51.914
- And then before going I
actually had an Australian friend

00:46:51.914 --> 00:46:55.470
here and she was like,
"Oh, Australians lie a lot.

00:46:55.470 --> 00:46:57.553
So watch out."
(Joey laughing)

00:46:57.553 --> 00:46:59.015
And then I think I told you.

00:46:59.015 --> 00:47:00.452
I was like, "My friend said,

00:47:00.452 --> 00:47:01.285
'Australians lie a lot.'"

00:47:01.285 --> 00:47:02.564
- No, no, no, nonsense.

00:47:02.564 --> 00:47:05.216
And then we told you about the drop bears.

00:47:05.216 --> 00:47:06.488
- I knew about the drop bears.

00:47:06.488 --> 00:47:08.055
- What is a drop bear?

00:47:08.055 --> 00:47:09.365
- Drop bears are like there's
a specific type of bear

00:47:09.365 --> 00:47:12.486
in Australia where they
drop from the tree.

00:47:12.486 --> 00:47:14.986
They drop down and attack you.

00:47:15.922 --> 00:47:16.755
When you're in Australia,

00:47:16.755 --> 00:47:18.195
you should never fall asleep under a tree

00:47:18.195 --> 00:47:20.283
because drop bear could
come down and attack you.

00:47:20.283 --> 00:47:21.694
- Unfortunately that is a lie as much-

00:47:21.694 --> 00:47:23.449
- No, no, no. It's absolutely real.

00:47:23.449 --> 00:47:24.597
And Meilyne believed me for a while.

00:47:24.597 --> 00:47:25.430
- I did not.

00:47:25.430 --> 00:47:26.263
- Yeah, you did.

00:47:26.263 --> 00:47:29.315
You were like, "Are they like
an actual species of bear?"

00:47:29.315 --> 00:47:31.761
- Where did the drop bear thing come from?

00:47:31.761 --> 00:47:32.829
- It's been around since like-

00:47:32.829 --> 00:47:35.904
- Every Australian I
swear I've met abroad,

00:47:35.904 --> 00:47:37.351
tells that story like on my first meeting.

00:47:37.351 --> 00:47:40.111
I'm just like, "Is this
just something the country

00:47:40.111 --> 00:47:42.812
has just agreed to tell the
entire rest of the world?"

00:47:42.812 --> 00:47:44.453
- Well 100s of Australians have died

00:47:44.453 --> 00:47:45.531
from drop bears every year.

00:47:45.531 --> 00:47:46.956
- Prove that Australia really exists.

00:47:46.956 --> 00:47:48.948
(Joey laughing)
Prove that it's not a lie.

00:47:48.948 --> 00:47:50.155
- I haven't seen it yet.

00:47:50.155 --> 00:47:50.988
- I haven't seen it.

00:47:50.988 --> 00:47:51.821
I have never been to Australia.

00:47:51.821 --> 00:47:52.654
Have you been to Australia?

00:47:52.654 --> 00:47:54.271
- Yeah, she's been.
- Have I?

00:47:54.271 --> 00:47:55.104
- Yeah.

00:47:55.104 --> 00:47:56.985
- She went on a flight
and she landed somewhere,

00:47:56.985 --> 00:47:58.261
that was called Australia.

00:47:58.261 --> 00:47:59.568
But that doesn't mean it exists.

00:47:59.568 --> 00:48:00.693
- There used to be a big gamer back

00:48:00.693 --> 00:48:02.232
in the day, right Meilyne?

00:48:02.232 --> 00:48:03.065
You used to play "MapleStory?"

00:48:03.065 --> 00:48:04.825
- Yeah, (laughs)

00:48:04.825 --> 00:48:06.431
so much.
(all laughing)

00:48:06.431 --> 00:48:07.924
- I was wondering where
that transition was going.

00:48:07.924 --> 00:48:10.812
- Wait, why did you
bring that up? (laughs)

00:48:10.812 --> 00:48:14.164
- Did you not talk to
people on "MapleStory?"

00:48:14.164 --> 00:48:15.497
- Oh yeah.
- People from other countries.

00:48:15.497 --> 00:48:17.996
- Yeah, my guild mother
was from Australia?

00:48:17.996 --> 00:48:20.054
- Did she lie a lot?

00:48:20.054 --> 00:48:20.969
- I don't think so.

00:48:20.969 --> 00:48:22.532
She told me about a lot of things.

00:48:22.532 --> 00:48:23.861
- Like the drop bears?

00:48:23.861 --> 00:48:25.490
- What's a guild mother?

00:48:25.490 --> 00:48:26.323
- I don't know.

00:48:26.323 --> 00:48:27.648
- It's the person who starts the guild.

00:48:27.648 --> 00:48:29.645
- It's pretty fucking self-explanatory.

00:48:29.645 --> 00:48:32.765
(all laughing)

00:48:32.765 --> 00:48:35.760
- I've never heard of it referred
to as a Guild mother yet.

00:48:35.760 --> 00:48:38.829
- It just happens that
online people in the games,

00:48:38.829 --> 00:48:41.271
they date each other and you
can get married in "MapleStory"

00:48:41.271 --> 00:48:42.857
and get crush rings or whatever.

00:48:42.857 --> 00:48:43.973
- Did you crush rings? (laughs)

00:48:43.973 --> 00:48:45.613
- Yeah, yeah.

00:48:45.613 --> 00:48:47.277
- So did you not have like questions

00:48:47.277 --> 00:48:49.348
about Australia for her?

00:48:49.348 --> 00:48:50.680
- Not so much.

00:48:50.680 --> 00:48:51.513
- Because I remember the first time

00:48:51.513 --> 00:48:52.653
I met an American friend,

00:48:52.653 --> 00:48:55.165
I asked them about so much shit.

00:48:55.165 --> 00:48:57.123
About just like, is it true that like.

00:48:57.123 --> 00:48:59.591
'Cause you know, in Australia-

00:48:59.591 --> 00:49:02.204
'Cause you only hear so
much from media, right?

00:49:02.204 --> 00:49:03.983
To the point where like,

00:49:03.983 --> 00:49:05.332
a lot of it is like over-glorified

00:49:05.332 --> 00:49:07.680
and sometimes just like a straight up lie.

00:49:07.680 --> 00:49:10.665
So like the first time I
met my American friend,

00:49:10.665 --> 00:49:11.774
through YouTube,

00:49:11.774 --> 00:49:13.081
I just asked them like
a shit ton of questions.

00:49:13.081 --> 00:49:14.348
Being like, "Is this true? Is this true?"

00:49:14.348 --> 00:49:17.940
- I did ask my Brazilian
friend about Brazil though,

00:49:17.940 --> 00:49:18.930
on "MapleStory."
- About what?

00:49:18.930 --> 00:49:20.799
- Did they really have big butts?

00:49:20.799 --> 00:49:21.971
- No, I asked them 'cause
there's this one case,

00:49:21.971 --> 00:49:25.803
the rumor or something
that kids are very violent

00:49:25.803 --> 00:49:27.566
when they get angry at
each other in games,

00:49:27.566 --> 00:49:28.399
they like kill each other.

00:49:28.399 --> 00:49:29.976
And one of the cases that
I was like checking out

00:49:29.976 --> 00:49:32.668
was this 13 year old that
stole a PS4 or something

00:49:32.668 --> 00:49:34.767
of his friend and the friend got angry,

00:49:34.767 --> 00:49:36.950
went over to his house with the machete,

00:49:36.950 --> 00:49:38.155
and just cut him in half.

00:49:38.155 --> 00:49:40.117
And I was like, "Oh, is that true?"

00:49:40.117 --> 00:49:42.984
And then my friend Tiago
was like, "Yeah, yeah.

00:49:42.984 --> 00:49:44.253
That happens all the
time. So I'm not sure."

00:49:44.253 --> 00:49:46.381
- Yeah, yeah. (laughs)

00:49:46.381 --> 00:49:47.446
- He didn't say yeah, yeah.

00:49:47.446 --> 00:49:51.207
He was like, "Yeah, that
happens a lot in ventrillo."

